      "id": "TEST-DRV-MOTOR-001",
      "before": {
        "workspaceId": "F:\\GitHub\\vice-sharp",
        "status": "closed",
        "title": "IecDriveMotorRampTests: 1541 motor ramp (5 tests)",
        "id": "TEST-DRV-MOTOR-001",
        "scopeStartLayerKey": "layer-1",
        "priority": "medium",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [],
        "condition": "After SetMotor(true) and 300,000 Tick() calls, MotorRotationCycles>0. Before 300,000, stays at 0. Motor off/on resets ramp. ReadSector(18,0) returns BAM bytes 0x12/0x01. 5 pass."
      },
      "after": {
        "workspaceId": "F:\\GitHub\\vice-sharp",
        "status": "pending",
        "title": "Native-oracle 1541 motor, rotation and sector-read acceptance",
        "id": "TEST-DRV-MOTOR-001",
        "scopeStartLayerKey": "layer-1",
        "priority": "medium",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          {
            "id": "ac-01",
            "text": "The AC-mapped fixture manifest covers motor off/on, unchanged repeated writes, on/off/on transitions, elapsed-clock boundaries, all four speed zones, byte-ready disabled/enabled and pending-edge cases. Use settled nonempty media for early-motion cases so an attachment delay cannot hide a fabricated 300000-cycle motor hold. Pin native source/build provenance and all initial/resource inputs.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-02",
            "text": "The manifest separately covers stateful attachment/read deadline minus one, exact deadline and plus one, followed by the next read; successful true-drive DOS access to track 18 sector 0; native-observed absent-media and unsuccessful reads; and buffered D64 byte access. Do not conflate the helper requirement at 300000 ticks with its historical 300001-tick test, or count that historical mismatch as accepted native behavior.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-03",
            "text": "Before production edits, every assertion passes with its independent correct mock and rejects a corresponding single-fault control inside a passing harness. Controls include the inserted 300000-cycle hold, erroneous origin reset on a repeated motor write, wrong speed-zone result, movement incorrectly gated by byte-ready enable, attachment/motor delay conflation, and wrong or missing bytes/status/ordered effects. No required case is skipped or unexecuted.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-04",
            "text": "After mock and review gates, bind exactly the same case inputs, expected outputs, assertion functions and interaction checks to the approved real native/managed adapters. Real true-drive tests must exercise drive CPU/VIA/DOS behavior; direct IecDrive.ReadSector or a manufactured counter cannot stand in for it. Preserve and separately report buffered-mode regression evidence.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-05",
            "text": "Retain chronological commands, input/source/ROM/media hashes, case-to-FR/TR/AC mapping, correct-mock and wrong-mock rejection results, full applicable suite denominators, production-bound traces and independent review receipts. Mock-only success or a historical five-pass statement cannot satisfy this TEST; all mandatory real-emulator, VSF and cumulative gates remain required.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          }
        ],
        "condition": "Validate native-derived motor/rotation and sector-read behavior through the actual managed true-drive dependency boundary. First prove the same assertions with discriminating correct and single-fault incorrect mocks in an all-green native-safe suite, then bind them to real managed/native adapters after the required acceptance gates. Preserve existing helper and buffer

