      "kind": "test",
      "id": "TEST-IEC-TIMING-001",
      "before": {
        "workspaceId": "F:\\GitHub\\vice-sharp",
        "status": "closed",
        "title": "IecTimingTests: ATN response within spec window (5 tests)",
        "id": "TEST-IEC-TIMING-001",
        "scopeStartLayerKey": "layer-1",
        "priority": "medium",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [],
        "condition": "After setting IecBus.Atn=false and calling Tick() up to 985 times, Clock==false and Data==false. After ATN release and Tick() up to 985 times, both return true. 5 pass."
      },
      "after": {
        "workspaceId": "F:\\GitHub\\vice-sharp",
        "status": "pending",
        "title": "Native-oracle C64 and VIC-20 IEC trace acceptance",
        "id": "TEST-IEC-TIMING-001",
        "scopeStartLayerKey": "layer-1",
        "priority": "medium",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          {
            "id": "ac-01",
            "text": "For each supported C64/VIC-20 region configuration in the approved native manifest, pin host/drive clocks, initial state, ROM/media, drive type and enable set. Enumerate all 64 combinations of the six single-drive Boolean control contributions (host ATN/DATA/CLK and drive ATNA/DATA/CLK), interpreted through that machine native pin polarity, plus no-drive, disabled-drive, and two-drive contention/release cases. Pin expected traces independently of managed output.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-02",
            "text": "For each machine adapter, exercise ATN assertion/release, repeated same-value writes, independent DATA/CLK updates and port reads at explicit ordered clock/phase checkpoints. Preserve native drive synchronization and VIA signaling side effects. Include direction-mask cases at the real host/drive VIA or CIA boundary; the C64 function alone is not VIC-20 coverage.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-03",
            "text": "Before production edits, correct mocks satisfy every mapped assertion and each planned single-fault control is rejected within a green native-safe suite. Controls include wrong polarity, omitted drive synchronization, omitted/duplicate VIA signal, unconditional paired line forcing, premature release under contention, wrong enable filtering, wrong event order and deadline-only acceptance of a shifted trace. No required case is skipped or unexecuted.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-04",
            "text": "After required mock/review gates, bind those exact cases, expected observations and assertion/interaction checks to the approved real C64 and xvic native adapters and actual managed connected-drive path. The standalone IecBus helper is not that path. Match the complete specified trace, not a count of tests or eventual line level inside 985 calls.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-05",
            "text": "Retain AC mapping and chronological mock, negative-control, real-adapter and cumulative suite receipts with exact counts, failures, skips and missing cases. Require all mapped real checks and mandatory emulator/VSF gates before satisfaction, plus independent HV acceptance; all unknown, unrun or mock-only outcomes remain unsatisfied.",
            "isSatisfied": false
          }
        ],
        "condition": "Validate the actual C64 and VIC-20 machine adapters and connected 1541 CPU/VIA IEC path against pinned native observations. Prove requirement-derived assertions with correct and single-fault wrong mocks first, green, then use the same fixtures/assertions on real implementations. Existing IecTimingTests helper results remain retained evidence but are not substitutes for native IEC trace comparison or shared-bus contention tests."
      },
      "changedFields": [
        "title",
